4202 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Main insight\072\nPerceived intelligence is shaped by how a system handles and communicates uncertainty\056 A system can distinguish between what it knows\054 what it infers\054 and what it still cannot determine\056 How much of that reasoning is shown to the user also changes how intelligent the system seems\056\n\nEvidence\050My system distinguishes between an Exact Date\054 a Selected Date\054 and an experience that Cannot Be Represented by one day\056 In the playtest\054 people also read hesitation\054 refusal\054 and apparent analysis as signs of intelligence\056\n\nLimit\050The prototype does not test whether the system actually understands\056 It tests how people interpret its behavior\056\n\nUnresolved question\050When does showing uncertainty make a system seem more intelligent\054 and when does it make it seem less capable\077)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 4203 0 R
     /Pg 4020 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

